            <ArticleTitle>[Idiopathic mesenteric phlebosclerosis: one case report and literature review].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-120</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11817/j.issn.1672-7347.2017.01.019</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Idiopathic mesenteric phlebosclerosis (IMP) is a rare disease and it is easy to be misdiagnosed, which is characterized by intestinal obstruction symptoms, such as abdominal pain, bloating and vomiting. In this study, a case of IMP was observed and the literatures were reviewed. Computed tomography shows funicular high-density shadow and vascular calcification shadow along the vessels around the bowels. Narrow band imaging (M-NBI) endoscopy revealed the disappeared honeycomb capillary, the disordered microvascular structure and the increased density of blood vessels.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
